    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d163">

                <pb facs="0308" n="220" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg220"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lincoln to Mr.
                            Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-06-17"><hi rendition="#italic">June 17, 1891</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 25.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 475.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>; Referring to your circular instruction of
                    May 8th inclosing copies of our new copyright act for communication to Her
                    Majesty’s Government, I have the honor to inclose herewith for your information
                    copies of my note transmitting the documents in question to the foreign office,
                    and of the reply thereto, which I have just received from the Marquis of
                    Salisbury.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Robert T.
                    Lincoln.</hi></signed></closer>



